==================================================
16. LARGE-SCALE GRAPH VISUALISATION
==================================================

The CoK may eventually contain
extremely large numbers of objects.

The visualiser must not load the
entire graph into RAM.

Instead, it uses:

- Query-driven subgraph extraction
- Lazy node expansion
- Depth-limited traversal
- Graph clustering
- Collapsed dependency groups
- Incremental rendering
- Viewport-based rendering
- Bounded visualisation memory

Additional nodes are retrieved from
local SSD or IPFS on demand.

Graph layout is presentation-only.

It does not change logical validity.


