38. ARCHITECTURAL INVARIANTS
==================================================

- Reasoning, ingestion and distribution
  are separate execution paths.

- The reasoner queries existing
  knowledge iteratively.

- Knowledge retrieval is bidirectional
  with the reasoning engine.

- The knowledge compiler does not sit
  in the main reasoning path.

- Neural interpretation and symbolic
  reasoning remain independent.

- Neural models are loaded on demand.

- Neural models may be unloaded
  after use.

- The reasoning engine does not
  require a resident LLM.

- Model parameter count is flexible.

- Quantised 3B models are supported
  when memory permits.

- Total runtime memory remains
  within the configured budget.

- Reasoning state survives model
  unloading.

- Knowledge uses a deterministic,
  machine-parsable DSL.

- The CoK supports directed
  hypergraph relationships.

- Human visualisation uses the same
  underlying knowledge objects.

- Graph layout does not change
  logical meaning.

- CPU-only operation remains supported.

- Knowledge archives remain modular,
  indexed and hot-swappable.

- IPFS is an optional storage backend.

- IPFS snapshots are immutable.

- Local journals provide writable overlays.

- Object IDs remain independent
  of IPFS CIDs.

- CID integrity is separate from
  knowledge correctness.

- Every derivation preserves
  assumptions, evidence and dependencies.

- Contradictions are not overwritten.

- Missing evidence is not proof
  of falsity.

- Failed search is not proof
  of impossibility.

- Offline operation remains possible
  with local dependencies.

- Public contributions require approval.

- Private data is never automatically
  published to IPFS.

- The reasoning graph can grow
  independently of neural model weights.


